{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Computing History and Object Oriented Programming"}, {"type": "position", "content": 12}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about computing history. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Learning Outcome"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation. Exchanges simple information on programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob12re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past of Verb to Be in Affirmative Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use<span class=\"strong\"> simple past of the verb to be </span>to talk about location, describe qualities or express feelings in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In <span class=\"strong\">TEXT </span>simple past, the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be </span>has two irregular forms. The conjugation changes according to the pronouns, we use <span class=\"strong\">was </span>with singular pronouns and <span class=\"strong\">were </span>with plural pronouns. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Computing<span class=\"strong\">was </span> very different in the mid-twentieth century. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Computer programs <span class=\"strong\">were </span>complex to use at the beginning.  </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is the structure you to build affirmative statements with the verb to be in simple past: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <span class=\"strong\">was/ were</span> + complement.</div>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb To Be in Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Pronoun\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"BE\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"were\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He / she / it\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We/They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"were\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "These two elements were essential to develop new technologies such as e-commerce and social networks "}, {"type": "example", "content": "In the 1950's, engineers used machine code languages, however, they were very complex and difficult to manipulate."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This paradigm was revolutionary because it allowed creating more evolved software components."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for an article about modern computing history."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Identify 5 main ideas about modern computing history."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Paraphrase these ideas and write a short text. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your text with a classmate. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for an article about modern computing history."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I identify 5 main ideas about modern computing history."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I paraphrase these ideas and write a short text."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my text with a partner.  "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past Tense in Affirmative Statements with Regular Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">simple past </span> to describe actions that happened in a specific time in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To make affirmative sentences in the <span class=\"strong\">simple past</span>, you should use verbs in past form:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <span class=\"strong\">Verb in Past </span>+ Complement.</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The first programming languages <span class=\"strong\">appeared </span>in the 50's. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">People <span class=\"strong\">started </span>to use email accounts in the 90's. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Verbs in past are classified in regular and irregular ones. The past form of <span class=\"strong\">regular verbs </span>is simple, you just need to add <span class=\"strong\">-d</span>, <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ied </span>at the end of the verb:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For those regular verbs that finish in <span class=\"strong\">\u2013e</span> or in <span class=\"strong\">vowel + y</span>,  you have to add <span class=\"strong\">\u2013d</span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> create \u2192 create<span class=\"strong\">d</span><br/>  manage \u2192 manag<span class=\"strong\">ed</span><br/>  play \u2192 play<span class=\"strong\">ed</span><br/>  </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When a regular verb finishes in <span class=\"strong\">\u2013d</span> or <span class=\"strong\">\u2013t</span>, you have to add <span class=\"strong\">\u2013ed</span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> invent \u2192 invent<span class=\"strong\">ed</span> <br/> mend \u2192 mend<span class=\"strong\">ed </span>  </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For those verbs that end in <span class=\"strong\">consonant + y</span>, you have to change the <span class=\"strong\">y</span> and add <span class=\"strong\">\u2013ied</span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> study \u2192 stud<span class=\"strong\"> ied </span><br/>  try \u2192 dr<span class=\"strong\"> ied </span>  </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Be careful, not all verbs are regular. <span class=\"strong\">Irregular verbs </span>can change in different forms, you need to practice them and memorize them, for example:  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> keep \u2192 <span class=\"strong\"> kept  </span> <br/> think \u2192 <span class=\"strong\"> thought </span> <br/> become \u2192 <span class=\"strong\"> became </span><br/>  </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "In the 1960's, mainframes appeared, these large machines were able to manage large volumes of information in an efficient way."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Years later, technology advanced and revolutionized communications."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Computer systems changed too. In the 1950's, engineers used machine code languages, however, they were very complex and difficult to manipulate."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Paraphrasing Information "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You <span class=\"strong\">paraphrase information of a text </span>when you want to express essential ideas in your own words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You paraphrase when you want to make a summary or add additional details to the information in a text.  When you are paraphrasing, you don't quote passages but you give your own understanding of the legitimate text."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the following chart, you can find some steps to paraphrase information effectively:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Read the text until you understand all the information.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Write down keywords or phrases that can remind about the essential information. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"3.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Make a draft writing your own ideas. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"4.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Check your draft and compare the accuracy of the information in comparison to the legitimate text.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"5.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use quotation marks to identify technical and unique information you take from the original text\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"6.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Write the name and author of the text if you want to use it as a bibliography for your paper.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mainframe "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "server computer "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Computing is constantly evolving. In the 1960's, mainframes appeared, these large machines were able to manage large volumes of information in an efficient way. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob12aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "programming paradigm"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "way you use to classify programming language within model computation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Then, in the 1970's, experts standardized the structured programming paradigm for complex software. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob12aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "machine code"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "program memory"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In the 1950's, engineers used machine code languages, however, they were very complex and difficult to manipulate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob12aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "word processor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "software application that allows you to create, edit and print documents"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: people had PC's at home for personal purposes such as the use of word processors or spreadsheet applications. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob12aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spreadsheet "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "program that calculates and organizes information in rows and columns"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: people had PC's at home for personal purposes such as the use of word processors or spreadsheet applications. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob12aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le01ob12re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob12re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "Computing is constantly evolving. In the 1960's, mainframes appeared, these large machines were able to manage large volumes of information in an efficient way. Not very long after, the concept of PC or personal computer started to be very important, organizations acquired more PC's to use administrative software, and people had PC's at home for personal purposes such as the use of word processors or spreadsheet applications."}, {"time": "33000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob12re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Years later, technology advanced and revolutionized communications. In 1989, the World Wide Web appeared together with the first web browser, and from that time, the communication by email became part of people's daily lives. These two elements were essential to develop new technologies such as e-commerce and social networks, and people had a better and faster access to information.\n</br></br>\nComputer systems changed too. In the 1950's, engineers used machine code languages, however, they were very complex and difficult to manipulate. Later, in the 1960's, high-level languages were famous because they were simple and helped in the development of more complex computer programs. Then, in the 1970's, experts standardized the structured programming paradigm for complex software, this paradigm divided programs into small components so they were easier to manage. However, the paradigm failed because it was difficult to understand how to create software or how to modify existing software."}, {"time": "107000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob12re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "In the 1990's, the object-oriented paradigm appeared, it developed ideas that were important for the use of Object Oriented Language. This paradigm was revolutionary because it allowed creating more evolved software components where it was possible to operate together software and data. </br>\nCertainly, software development ideas and computing are still changing and they will keep innovating."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le01ob12re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "_data": [], "id": 3, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n2le01ob12re5vsc01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can understand written information about some facts in computing history. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the origins of object oriented programming."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can paraphrase information from a text."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why do you think computing evolves that fast?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What changes in computing do you think were the most important during the XX century? Why?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "As computing evolved, machines were more complex. "}], "id": 0, "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]